00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:47.860
And when we were
planning out our chatbot,

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.560
one thing that we rapidly
came to the conclusion of

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.900
is that no chatbot is an island.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.910
So while a chatbot--

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:58.300
you can build an experience
just purely as a chatbot,

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.580
it's much more powerful
in the application

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.860
when we apply it with
other technologies

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.860
and other back ends, so being
able to service the things

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.080
that the users want
integrated seamlessly

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.680
with both stuff in the cloud,
and potentially, on premise.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.650
And for that, what you
need is a platform.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.510
If you define a
platform, it's a group

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.570
of technologies that are used
to base other technologies

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.150
and applications on top of.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:24.070
So what we needed was a
platform that could serve all

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:27.280
of our needs around both the
machine learning aspects--

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.160
around Dialogflow itself, around
natural language understanding,

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.000
et cetera--

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.890
but also, getting data
from other sources,

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:38.290
whether that's internal
or within the cloud.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.200
And this is the current
working platform

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:45.100
that we put together
when working with James.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.010
On your right-hand side,
